@module loader ; The SpeedLock 7 loader: the notice, the block reader, the stage at $BF0D
@about LoaderStart checks for a Multiface, prints the copyright notice and clears the memory the chain used, then loads the second stage (tape block 7) at $BF0D and runs it. The block reader LoadBlocks reads a pilot of its own timing, the sync pulses and the bytes, each stored as (byte XOR k) + a by StoreByte (the operands are the keys, rewritten by the tape's blocks 17 and 19); BlockTable walks the blocks to their banks. While it waits for edges it runs a task through the pointer at $BDB7: the attribute reveal and the countdown.
@about c1: LoaderStart at frame 2288; the stage entered at frame 2484; the last block read by frame 23856; the bootstrap entered at frame 23974 (docs/03 3.1).

$B8F9 c LoaderStart ; Check for a Multiface, clear the RAM, print the notice and load the stage
> Interrupts off, SP = $BFFF. IN A,($3F) and IN A,($9F) are the Multiface's page-in ports: if either pages a ROM in, the byte at $0000 is no longer the 128K ROM's DI ($F3) and JP $0000 restarts the machine. The OUTs to $1F, $7B and $BB page such interfaces out again. Then PrintNotice and LoaderMain. Known from the code; c1: L1 1.

$B935 c PrintNotice ; Print the copyright notice: the bars and the strings of NoticeText

$B96C c DrawBar ; Draw a bar of A cells at the screen position BC, bright red attributes

$B995 c PrintChar ; Print the character A (from $20) with the ROM font at $3D00

$B9B1 c DrawGlyph ; Copy the 8 bytes at HL to the screen cell DE, white attribute

$B9CD c CellAddress ; DE = the screen address of row B, column C

$B9E2 c PrintString ; Print the string at HL up to a zero, from row B column C, wrapping at column 32

$B9FB t NoticeText ; The copyright notice and the FAST warning, zero-ended strings
> Read by PrintString (c1: L1 reads). Shown during the whole load.

$BBF4 c WaitTask ; The task the edge loop runs while it waits: the attribute reveal, then the countdown
> LoadBlocks calls it between two edges (CALL $BBF4 at $BDB6); the task's own code is reached through the pointer at $BDB7, which each step rewrites. Known from the code; the screen shows the attributes coming in and a countdown at the top right in c1.

$BCF2 c LdEdge2 ; Two edges: sample the EAR bit until it changes, twice

$BD13 c LoadBlocks ; Read the pilot, the sync and the bytes of a block to IX, DE bytes

$BD9C c StoreByte ; Store a byte: (L XOR k) + a, k and a the operands of this code
> The tape's block 17 rewrites k ($BD9D: $C1, then $86); a ($BDA0) stays $11. src/tape/side1.txt and tools/mktape.py use the same operands in the other direction.

$BDD0 c StoreLast ; Store the last byte of a block the same way, with its own operands (block 19 rewrites them)

$BE47 c ReadMark ; Read the bits of a mark between two blocks

$BE5D c TimeCheck ; Measure the tape's edges into TimeBuffer and compare them (replaced by tape block 37)

$BEDF c LoadEnd ; The end of a stream of blocks: the XOR in H must be 0

$BEEA c LoaderMain ; Clear $5D00-$BBF3 (the chain), load the stage at $BF0D, clear the screen and run it
